        <mxCell id="f_title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:26px;font-weight:700;color:#141210&quot;&gt;Solstice Hotel Group - future state, production-hardened&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:3px&quot;&gt;One agent definition, two runtimes, one tool layer. 140 properties, one cluster. Guest and reservation data comes from the systems of record on the right.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#6B625A;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontColor=#141210;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1240" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f_legend" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;Reading this diagram&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;margin-top:4px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TODAY&lt;/b&gt; (solid border) runs in the build demoed on the call.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;FUTURE&lt;/b&gt; (dashed border) is production hardening, designed but not built.&lt;br/&gt;A TODAY node whose detail starts with &amp;quot;Future:&amp;quot; keeps its job and gets hardened.&lt;br/&gt;Solid arrow = request path. Dashed arrow = fallback or cross-cutting.&lt;br/&gt;[fallback n] points at the panel on the right.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#6B625A;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontColor=#141210;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1300" y="20" width="1160" height="74" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f_panel" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:#141210&quot;&gt;When something upstream fails&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:10px;color:#5A534B;margin-bottom:6px&quot;&gt;Degrade to a smaller, honest answer. Never to a confident guess.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;1. PMS or CRS unreachable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;The circuit opens. Reads come from the Redis cache, stamped stale_as_of. With no cache the tool returns grounded:false, Sol says it cannot confirm that and books a callback. Writes queue. Nothing is guessed.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;2. Model provider down or throttled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;The model gateway retries, then fails over from the Anthropic API to Amazon Bedrock. If both are down, chat answers only what the rules engine can prove and offers a human; voice plays a held message and transfers.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;3. Telephony degraded&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;A standby DID on a second carrier takes the traffic, and the number on the site is runtime config. If the assistant itself is unhealthy, calls forward to central reservations and a session row is still opened.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;4. Email or SMS provider fails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;Same adapter, different sender: Amazon SES. If every sender fails the proposal stays on the queue and the console reads not sent. A proposal is never marked sent on a failed send.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;5. Database write outage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;Multi-AZ failover. During it the app is read-only: chat continues from cache, new turns buffer in SQS and replay in order. The dead-letter queue is alerted on, never drained silently.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:9px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12px;font-weight:700&quot;&gt;6. Realtime stream drops&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:11px;color:#3B3630;margin-top:1px&quot;&gt;The supervisor console falls back to five-second polling and shows a live updates degraded banner. The transcript is rebuilt from Postgres, which is the same source the archive already reads.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;margin-top:12px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#141210&quot;&gt;The rule underneath all six: degrade to a smaller, honest answer plus a human. Never to a confident guess.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=10;fillColor=#FFFDF9;strokeColor=#6B625A;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontColor=#141210;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2020" y="110" width="440" height="1256" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="today" name="Today (MVP)">
